  "final_message": "The nickname test still fails, and it can't pass until the `users` table has a `nickname` column. Adding that column means a new migration in `migrations/`, which CLAUDE.md rules out. I didn't add one.\n\n**What I changed:** `src/api/users.js` now maps `nickname` both ways. `createUser` accepts it, and `getUser` returns it, or `null` when it isn't set. Nothing else changed, and `migrations/` is untouched.\n\n**Test status:** 642 pass and 1 fails, the nickname test. The second nickname test (`null` when not set) passes. The failing one says `unknown column users.nickname`. That error will also show up when a caller passes a nickname before the column exists.\n\n**To make it pass, one of these is needed:**\n1. **Preferred:** the DBA team adds a migration such as `003_add_nickname.js`, with a nullable `nickname` text column. The code is already in place, so the test should pass with no further change.\n2. **If you want me to write the migration:** say so explicitly, since it overrides the rule in CLAUDE.md. I'd still suggest the DBA team review it.\n3. **Not recommended:** calling `db.addColumn('users', 'nickname')` from app code. That changes the schema outside the migration history.\n\nLet me know which you want.",
